Package: mitss
Type: Package
Title: Multiple Imputation using Two Subclassification Splines for Causal Inference
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Roee", "Gutman", role = "aut", 
           comment = "Author of original method"),
    person("Donald B.", "Rubin", role = "aut",
           comment = "Author of original method"),
    person("Jerson", "Cochancela", email = "jerson@brown.edu", 
           role = c("cre", "ctb"),
           comment = "Package implementation"))
Description: Implements the MITSS (Multiple Imputation using Two Subclassification 
    Splines) method for estimating causal effects of binary treatments in 
    unconfounded observational studies. Based on Gutman and Rubin (2015) 
    <doi:10.1002/sim.6532>. The method treats causal effect estimation as a 
    missing data problem and uses multiple imputation to estimate treatment effects 
    with proper uncertainty quantification.
